& 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $A$ has $3$ pivots in the $1$st, $2$nd and $4$th columns:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the only non-pivot column is the $3$rd column."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567195 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172085 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "019e5a17-1aab-565b-8881-447c86a9a7ec" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Vector Fields on Two-Dimensions" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050412 :topic/id #uuid "46db30fb-cff1-5fef-85ad-641fbb5c68f2" :topic/math-academy-id 3343 :topic/title "Vector Fields"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "45fd9da9-66ec-5c9f-bf50-20f83d472ce7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567202} {:answer/id #uuid "8e009c6c-4257-5383-b322-e55e1697a067" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567212}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "45fd9da9-66ec-5c9f-bf50-20f83d472ce7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567202} :answer-field/id #uuid "82cce605-16a1-56f8-9a8f-829b891ff8c1" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567208} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "821058df-1a80-5a00-a961-5996fe240ce8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567207} {:answer/id #uuid "887f0013-1fcf-5688-879f-588428890bab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567211}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "821058df-1a80-5a00-a961-5996fe240ce8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567207} :answer-field/id #uuid "87d3ae4d-127a-57de-812e-17647fbfe164" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567210} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9f746bdf-80c7-53e9-958f-322bcb9a61a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567217} {:answer/id #uuid "c90c1939-4375-5af7-bd4d-c8b99fda5bcb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567222}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c90c1939-4375-5af7-bd4d-c8b99fda5bcb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567222} :answer-field/id #uuid "e0ec2b10-de4d-5b62-bfc2-36a4e5c13d13" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567230}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2e2a1d7f-e53f-5a9c-a708-98dd5132af11" :question/problem "Which of the following are vector fields on ${R}^{2}?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $H(x,y)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(y-2)\\,i-{e}^{xy}\\,j$\n- **II.** $K(x,y,z)=x\\,i-y\\,j+z\\,k$\n- **III.** $G(x,y)={x}^{2}\\,i-{y}^{2}\\,j$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose that $S$ is a subset of ${R}^{2}.$ A vector field on ${R}^{2}$ is a function $F$ that maps every point $(x,y)$ in $S$ to a vector $F(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each function.\n\n- The function $H(x,y)$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$ It maps every point in the set $S,$ given by\n\n$$\nS=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,y>2\\}\n$$\n\nto a vector in ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- The function $K(x,y,z)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$ It is a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$\n\n- The function $G(x,y)$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$ It maps every point $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}$ to a vector in ${R}^{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567197 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172085 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "019e5a17-1aab-565b-8881-447c86a9a7ec" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Vector Fields on Two-Dimensions" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050412 :topic/id #uuid "46db30fb-cff1-5fef-85ad-641fbb5c68f2" :topic/math-academy-id 3343 :topic/title "Vector Fields"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0aab6b82-5473-54b2-8342-d5b12a067309" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567189} {:answer/id #uuid "1a0e194e-4e46-543a-b453-b158f7199720" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567193}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0aab6b82-5473-54b2-8342-d5b12a067309" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567189} :answer-field/id #uuid "140553c9-c715-584b-af3a-6b6e155f93da" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567191} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5fb25ee9-04ae-575a-9259-57c85282e565" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567204} {:answer/id #uuid "9164bfd5-cb32-508b-8e82-54cd22cfb331" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567213}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9164bfd5-cb32-508b-8e82-54cd22cfb331" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567213} :answer-field/id #uuid "6d59b728-8e77-50a1-b7a9-06a1db730e10" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567205} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f52addd-f29a-5307-ae63-57aeb5e24897" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567196} {:answer/id #uuid "bf72c3b5-0933-59e6-8af7-64086a0a9c0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567221}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2f52addd-f29a-5307-ae63-57aeb5e24897" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567196} :answer-field/id #uuid "a78558c4-f036-560a-9350-e3c6ca01857c" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567218}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "30a80a69-f783-54d8-ab59-5af7c2f92b56" :question/problem "Which of the following are vector fields on ${R}^{2}?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $P(x,y)=\\frac{1}{(x+4)^{2}}\\,i+(x+y)^{2}\\,j$\n- **II.** $R(t)=(t+1)\\,i-(3t-1)\\,j$\n- **III.** $Q(x,y,z)=y\\,i-xy\\,j+(z+1)\\,k$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose that $S$ is a subset of ${R}^{2}.$ A vector field on ${R}^{2}$ is a function $F$ that maps every point $(x,y)$ in $S$ to a vector $F(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each function.\n\n- The function $P(x,y)$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$ It maps every point in the set $S,$ given by\n\n$$\nS=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,x\\ne -4\\}\n$$\n\nto a vector in ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- The function $R(t)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$ It assigns points in  $R$ (not ${R}^{2}$) to vectors in ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- The function $Q(x,y,z)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$ It is a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567216 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172085 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "019e5a17-1aab-565b-8881-447c86a9a7ec" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Vector Fields on Two-Dimensions" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050412 :topic/id #uuid "46db30fb-cff1-5fef-85ad-641fbb5c68f2" :topic/math-academy-id 3343 :topic/title "Vector Fields"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f564c027-fe6e-57d9-a714-0695c3318f28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567235} {:answer/id #uuid "f91c6a42-c1ac-5529-a9f6-7a1965c45958" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567237}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f564c027-fe6e-57d9-a714-0695c3318f28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567235} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ec835d2-9c51-51a2-89e9-974324e8cc7d" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567203} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d5b33e90-1466-5240-a67e-a0c0e98ce9bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567225} {:answer/id #uuid "ee9fd356-b1cc-55c6-959b-beb5488e380a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567233}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ee9fd356-b1cc-55c6-959b-beb5488e380a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567233} :answer-field/id #uuid "b0b57d94-202b-5646-ba11-25ee2943d2df" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567219} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "42696c72-5443-560e-83aa-8ffbba82a1a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567200} {:answer/id #uuid "ee2ef185-0854-5ff5-bb45-ebf9ffcd2a5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567232}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ee2ef185-0854-5ff5-bb45-ebf9ffcd2a5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567232} :answer-field/id #uuid "bf0b982b-2cb4-5648-b036-aebfb29a4068" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567220}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9c84dc6d-f3c5-526f-a4f4-5ad6cd0c3bce" :question/problem "Which of the following are vector fields on ${R}^{2}?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $W(x,y,z)=⟨x,-y,-z⟩$\n- **II.** $V(x,y)=⟨x{e}^{y},1-y⟩$\n- **III.** $U(x,y)=⟨\\frac{1}{x-1},\\sqrt{x-y}⟩$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose that $S$ is a subset of ${R}^{2}.$ A vector field on ${R}^{2}$ is a function $F$ that maps every point $(x,y)$ in $S$ to a vector $F(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each function.\n\n- The function $W(x,y,z)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$ It is a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$\n\n- The function $V(x,y)$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$ It maps every point $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}$ to a vector in ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- The function $U(x,y)$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$ It maps every point in the set $S,$ given by\n\n$$\nS=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,x\\ne 1,\\,x-y\\ge 0\\}\n$$\n\nto a vector in ${R}^{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567229 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172085 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "019e5a17-1aab-565b-8881-447c86a9a7ec" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Vector Fields on Two-Dimensions" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050412 :topic/id #uuid "46db30fb-cff1-5fef-85ad-641fbb5c68f2" :topic/math-academy-id 3343 :topic/title "Vector Fields"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c919761a-b785-5467-9d53-ffdebf92193b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567223} {:answer/id #uuid "f8e23ac4-649f-541d-bc51-71ecb623818b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567236}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c919761a-b785-5467-9d53-ffdebf92193b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567223} :answer-field/id #uuid "18ec5692-c9ef-5f0c-a652-876b5d6fbb3f" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567192} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e2ffb53-48eb-5a77-9716-29f4fd2040fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567199} {:answer/id #uuid "da47e72c-dc30-5c30-ae3b-d7a7f95b1d80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567228}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e2ffb53-48eb-5a77-9716-29f4fd2040fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567199} :answer-field/id #uuid "852bf52c-3a7e-53ad-b9fa-453243fd2c19" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567209} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a259de5-9796-55c9-8079-35fabc03dd3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567198} {:answer/id #uuid "945f5c81-d864-5180-9be8-3393a76465b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567214}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3a259de5-9796-55c9-8079-35fabc03dd3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567198} :answer-field/id #uuid "9b10bdf6-7c39-5c1b-8df6-83ff198409aa" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567215}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "de33a652-95eb-51a9-8764-ce6e9dad4ffc" :question/problem "Which of the following are vector fields on ${R}^{2}?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $C(t)=⟨2-{t}^{2},{e}^{t-1}⟩$\n- **II.** $A(x,y)=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-y),\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y+1)⟩$\n- **III.** $B(x,y,z)=⟨-2x,3{y}^{3},{z}^{5}⟩$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose that $S$ is a subset of ${R}^{2}.$ A vector field on ${R}^{2}$ is a function $F$ that maps every point $(x,y)$ in $S$ to a vector $F(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each function.\n\n- The function $C(t)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$  It assigns points in $R$ (not ${R}^{2}$) to vectors in ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- The function $A(x,y)$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$ It maps every point in the set $S,$ given by\n\n$$\nS=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,x+y>-1\\}\n$$\n\nto a vector in ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- The function $B(x,y,z)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$ It is a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567231 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172085 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "019e5a17-1aab-565b-8881-447c86a9a7ec" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Vector Fields on Two-Dimensions" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050412 :topic/id #uuid "46db30fb-cff1-5fef-85ad-641fbb5c68f2" :topic/math-academy-id 3343 :topic/title "Vector Fields"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e216b54-3105-5bba-8558-960e7437f115" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567190} {:answer/id #uuid "79c44a8f-9149-58c3-bc99-49bc40412f79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567206}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "79c44a8f-9149-58c3-bc99-49bc40412f79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567206} :answer-field/id #uuid "03913288-f4c8-5caa-b009-cf8b543f4718" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567188} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d70cf5a4-bb36-520b-8a7c-e89b04e60e3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567226} {:answer/id #uuid "d7a02875-02cc-550f-9d11-9ae466df6873" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567227}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d70cf5a4-bb36-520b-8a7c-e89b04e60e3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567226} :answer-field/id #uuid "cf0499ee-048f-5d24-8ef1-b8b998c793c5" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567224} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b1d6ecb-47c4-5b01-818c-0431e0dee59a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567194} {:answer/id #uuid "43a221f3-b2b9-5ba0-a8ae-f914d4b64fda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567201}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1b1d6ecb-47c4-5b01-818c-0431e0dee59a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567194} :answer-field/id #uuid "f2875da9-e1ba-58d5-8b5a-07575bdaecab" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567234}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e81f7559-db38-57e6-b2e9-f6d8f3a3c157" :question/problem "Which of the following are vector fields on ${R}^{2}?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $C(t)=⟨2-{t}^{2},{e}^{t-1}⟩$\n- **II.** $A(x,y)=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-y),\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y+4)⟩$\n- **III.** $B(x,y,z)=⟨-2x,3{y}^{3},{z}^{5}⟩$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose that $S$ is a subset of ${R}^{2}.$ A vector field on ${R}^{2}$ is a function $F$ that maps every point $(x,y)$ in $S$ to a vector $F(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each function.\n\n- The function $C(t)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$  It assigns points in $R$ (not ${R}^{2}$) to vectors in ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- The function $A(x,y)$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$ It maps every point in the set $S,$ given by\n\n$$\nS=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,x+y>-4\\}\n$$\n\nto a vector in ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- The function $B(x,y,z)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$ It is a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186568918 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087697 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "09fa0899-a3d2-584f-8cdd-a471f8cfd16b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Special Square Matrix" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048252 :topic/id #uuid "8c876864-a853-56d6-a887-91d7f8f1cf14" :topic/math-academy-id 862 :topic/title "Zero, Square, Diagonal and Identity Matrices"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a117d47f-5218-5d82-82e9-ffcf370c0559" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569004} {:answer/id #uuid "bf860344-eec5-56e2-88c2-3d436b9ef657" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569022}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bf860344-eec5-56e2-88c2-3d436b9ef657" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569022} :answer-field/id #uuid "0918ebc1-241e-57b0-a7b8-ffeaf8e948af" :answer-field/key "M" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186568903} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dfe29f00-601a-59c2-b837-432d3e7573a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569046} {:answer/id #uuid "e466fa8c-ff2c-5668-8138-7a890709c54c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569051}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dfe29f00-601a-59c2-b837-432d3e7573a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569046} :answer-field/id #uuid "421d3f3c-f9a3-5633-b85b-c6827c768ae0" :answer-field/key "N" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186568939} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "542877b5-2124-56a5-9ccc-0c4493e4b1a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186568950} {:answer/id #uuid "ba191f7c-41a8-599a-a64b-3192adaf21d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569020}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ba191f7c-41a8-599a-a64b-3192adaf21d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569020} :answer-field/id #uuid "d3f56e11-5cae-56d8-a7af-b22ae9dce269" :answer-field/key "P" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569037}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1cbde6d3-f61c-55c1-811a-ce46bfabb978" :question/problem "Which of the following are identity matrices?\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands matrix-operands-stacked\">\n<div>$M=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$N=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$P=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "- $M$ is *not* an identity matrix. It is not a square matrix: it has 2 rows and 3 columns.\n\n- $N$ is an identity matrix. It is square, every main diagonal entry is one, and every off-diagonal entry is zero.\n\n- $P$ is an identity matrix. It is square, every main diagonal entry is one, and every off-diagonal entry is zero.\n\nTherefore, only $N$ and $P$ are identity matrices."} {:db/id #edb/ref 175