5499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569032} :answer-field/id #uuid "f88d7264-a83a-5d0d-8f4b-b745cd9361d6" :answer-field/key "M" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569058}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "346bfa25-2542-5ec3-809a-ea74dfd72cbe" :question/problem "Which of the following are diagonal matrices?\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands matrix-operands-stacked\">\n<div>$F=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$H=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 0 & 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$M=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "- $F$ is a diagonal matrix. It is square and every off-diagonal entry is zero. It is also an identity matrix; identity matrices are diagonal matrices.\n\n- $H$ is *not* a diagonal matrix. It is square, but an entry off the main diagonal is nonzero: ${h}_{14}=7\\ne 0$.\n\n- $M$ is *not* a diagonal matrix. It is not a square matrix: it has 4 rows and 2 columns.\n\nTherefore, only $F$ is a diagonal matrix."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186568937 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087697 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "09fa0899-a3d2-584f-8cdd-a471f8cfd16b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Special Square Matrix" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048252 :topic/id #uuid "8c876864-a853-56d6-a887-91d7f8f1cf14" :topic/math-academy-id 862 :topic/title "Zero, Square, Diagonal and Identity Matrices"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "645fb2a9-5ab8-5a39-a0b1-2730820c4782" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186568963} {:answer/id #uuid "e24b7ce1-4e1e-500e-