r/id #uuid "f3854d29-f6c0-5f38-92ce-58e740817991" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186574552 :task-item/_responses [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186574143 :task-item/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573261} :task-item/status {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045571}}]} :answer-field/id #uuid "153fc202-de5e-501a-8466-13be4cac24dc" :answer-field/key "Column 4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186574758}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0dd8f23a-a284-5af7-a370-b6877f8aea89" :question/math-academy-id "q-73637" :question/problem "What are the pivot columns of the matrix $P,$ given by\n\n$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, we need to convert $P$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $P$ has $3$ pivots. In particular, the pivot columns are the $1$st, $3$rd, and $4$th columns." :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049723 :topic/id #uuid "0e15397e-6c32-508c-b6ea-90f1a9e5a237" :topic/math-academy-id 1904 :topic/title "Identifying the Pivot Columns of a Matrix"} :activity/title "Identifying the Pivot Columns of a Matrix" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572820} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573341}] :task-item/_content [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186574143 :task-item/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573261} :task-item/elapsed-seconds 14.362 :task-item/id #uuid "37d2e5e2