\\left(4 x \\right)}\\right)\\prime \\\\ &=\\frac{1}{4 x}\\cdot 4 \\\\ &=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ &\\not\\equiv \\frac{1}{2 x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Substituting $y=\\ln{\\left(4 x \\right)}$ and $y\\prime=\\frac{1}{x}$ into the original equation gives an identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y\\prime &\\overset{?}{=}4 e^{- y} \\\\ \\frac{1}{x} &\\overset{?}{=}\\frac{4}{e^{\\ln{\\left(4 x \\right)}}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{x} &=\\frac{1}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statement II is true, the function $y=\\ln{\\left(4 x \\right)}$ is a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186577218 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100888 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "201edc93-37b4-556a-aaea-4fcf9a01077a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Solution to a First-Order Differential Equation" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049486 :topic/id #uuid "f8bc5d87-e505-5270-9efd-ad77aaf46e52" :topic/math-academy-id 1181 :topic/title "Verifying Solutions of Differential Equations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5cc87408-521e-5ff3-81ad-d12b8336cba2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577198} {:answer/id #uuid "ee5cc371-1e31-5af0-b590-b0e123a69dca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577226}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5cc87408-521e-5ff3-81ad-d12b8336cba2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577198} :answer-field/id #uuid "121ca29b-ff12-50d2-a3bf-d408737a7afb" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577183} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11a41b91-a3e8-52ba-ba25-b21d70c222a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577182} {:answer/id #uuid "83796f1a-f177-5bfb-9026-ee69e4168ca1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577210}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "83796f1a-f177-5bfb-9026-ee69e4168ca1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577210} :answer-field/id #uuid "2a41cff6-b393-54f3-8621-68b284e47ac3" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577189} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34812337-a6dc-5027-b32a-f77570a6742e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577191} {:answer/id #uuid "45dea541-accf-5351-87dd-ce5e1122aee6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577196}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "34812337-a6dc-5027-b32a-f77570a6742e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577191} :answer-field/id #uuid "f98785b4-f724-5466-bb66-b99672465add" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577228}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d568f072-4f2d-5062-9df6-070b49ac30ab" :question/problem "Consider the following differential equation.\n\n$$\ny\\prime=- 5 \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)}\n$$\n\nLet $f(x)=\\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $f\\prime(x)=- 2 \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)}.$\n- **II.** Substituting $y=f(x)$ and $y\\prime=f\\prime(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement.\n- **III.** The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation." :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in an interval where the function is defined and the equation is valid.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Differentiating $f(x)=\\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f\\prime(x)&=\\left(\\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}\\right)\\prime \\\\ &=-\\sin(4x)\\cdot 4 \\\\ &=- 4 \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)} \\\\ &\\not\\equiv - 2 \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Substituting $y=\\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}$ and $y\\prime=- 4 \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)}$ into the original equation gives expressions that are not identical:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y\\prime &\\overset{?}{=}- 5 \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)} \\\\ - 4 \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)} &\\not\\equiv - 5 \\sin{\\left(4 x \\right)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since statement II is false, the function $y=\\cos{\\left(4 x \\right)}$ is not a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186577227 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100888 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "201edc93-37b4-556a-aaea-4fcf9a01077a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Solution to a First-Order Differential Equation" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049486 :topic/id #uuid "f8bc5d87-e505-5270-9efd-ad77aaf46e52" :topic/math-academy-id 1181 :topic/title "Verifying Solutions of Differential Equations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "217f4b64-d556-5199-9baf-43913544c7a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #ed