/id #edb/ref 17592186577193} :answer-field/id #uuid "d23c64dd-d8d6-5fdd-aced-ed924c331a79" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577217}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f69906ca-c5a8-50c6-b2ca-cd97ea4fc11a" :question/problem "Consider the following differential equation.\n\n$$\ny\\prime=\\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}\n$$\n\nLet $f(x)=\\frac{\\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{4}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $f\\prime(x)=\\frac{\\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{2}.$\n- **II.** Substituting $y=f(x)$ and $y\\prime=f\\prime(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement.\n- **III.** The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation." :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in an interval where the function is defined and the equation is valid.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Differentiating $f(x)=\\frac{\\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{4},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f\\prime(x)&=\\left(\\frac{\\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{4}\\right)\\prime \\\\ &=\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 2\\cos(2x) \\\\ &=\\frac{\\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Substituting $y=\\frac{\\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{4}$ and $y\\prime=\\frac{\\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{2}$ into the original equation gives expressions that are not identical:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y\\prime &\\overset{?}{=}\\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)} \\\\ \\frac{\\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{2} &\\not\\equiv \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since statement II is false, the function $y=\\frac{\\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}}{4}$ is not a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186577232 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100888 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "201edc93-37b4-556a-aaea-4fcf9a01077a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Solution to a First-Order Differential Equation" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049486 :topic/id #uuid "f8bc5d87-e505-5270-9efd-ad77aaf46e52" :topic/math-academy-id 1181 :topic/title "Verifying Solutions of Differential Equations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "899c8195-18d6-577b-b497-a767c94fd9ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577260} {:answer/id #uuid "e2508ccb-9092-5e29-b099-8e7a5e084a7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577276}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "899c8195-18d6-577b-b497-a767c94fd9ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577260} :answer-field/id #uuid "2f0af7fc-a183-5432-8aa6-90714a3b16d0" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577239} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "309fec51-949f-5aa2-9e56-7b7ab05da2dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577240} {:answer/id #uuid "836fdad7-3107-5b59-aeb6-c89477568106" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577259}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "309fec51-949f-5aa2-9e56-7b7ab05da2dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577240} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d5507b0-90fc-51e0-a572-7ef2530af52e" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577244} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "144251c2-9709-58d2-a1b8-7cfd771764df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577234} {:answer/id #uuid "2cb86bec-67e2-5f02-9a89-601383bc948d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577238}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "144251c2-9709-58d2-a1b8-7cfd771764df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577234} :answer-field/id #uuid "b172cfd8-30ff-5646-9672-925044e7beef" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577269}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "08c38953-f704-56cc-b3e1-73f07fd4a27c" :question/problem "Consider the following differential equation.\n\n$$\ny\\prime=\\frac{5 y}{x},\\qquad x\\ne 0\n$$\n\nLet $f(x)=- 4 x^{5}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $f\\prime(x)=- 16 x^{4}.$\n- **II.** Substituting $y=f(x)$ and $y\\prime=f\\prime(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement.\n- **III.** The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation." :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in an interval where the function is defined and the equation is valid.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Differentiating $f(x)=- 4 x^{5},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f\\prime(x)&=\\left(- 4 x^{5}\\right)\\prime \\\\ &=-4\\cdot 5 x^{4} \\\\ &=- 20 x^{4} \\\\ &\\not\\equiv - 16 x^{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Substituting $y=- 4 x^{5}$ and $y\\prime=- 20 x^{4}$ into the original equation gives an identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y\\prime &\\overset{?}{=}\\frac{5 y}{x} \\\\ - 20 x^{4} &\\overset{?}{=}\\frac{5\\left(- 4 x^{5}\\right)}{x} \\\\ - 20 x^{4} &=- 20 x^{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statement II is true, the function $y=- 4 x^{5}$ is a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186577237 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100888 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "201edc93-37b4-556a-aaea-4fcf9a01077a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Solution to a First-Order Differential Equation" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049486 :topic/id #uuid "f8bc5d87-e505-5270-9efd-ad77aaf46e52" :topic/math-academy-id 1181 :topic/title "Verifying Solutions of Differential Equations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "096fa35e-adf0-56ac-96a6-f0d914653171" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577233} {:answer/id #uuid "702a4e6a-ff6b-521c-a157-521109dc3428" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577254}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "096fa35e-adf0-56ac-96a6-f0d914653171" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577233} :answer-field/id #uuid "14afc219-898a-5f29-a488-e9de74e30fc4" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577235} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32789ef3-e490-5af2-bd76-0010e6157806" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/re