ial equation." :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in an interval where the function is defined and the equation is valid.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Differentiating $f(x)=- 8 x^{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f\\prime(x)&=\\left(- 8 x^{2}\\right)\\prime \\\\ &=-8\\cdot 2 x \\\\ &=- 16 x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Substituting $y=- 8 x^{2}$ and $y\\prime=- 16 x$ into the original equation gives expressions that are not identical:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y\\prime &\\overset{?}{=}\\frac{5 y}{x} \\\\ - 16 x &\\overset{?}{=}\\frac{5\\left(- 8 x^{2}\\right)}{x} \\\\ - 16 x &\\not\\equiv - 40 x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since statement II is false, the function $y=- 8 x^{2}$ is not a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186577247 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100888 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "201edc93-37b4-556a-aaea-4fcf9a01077a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Solution to a First-Order Differential Equation" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049486 :topic/id #uuid "f8bc5d87-e505-5270-9efd-ad77aaf46e52" :topic/math-academy-id 1181 :topic/title "Verifying Solutions of Differential Equations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c669eed-d1b3-5024-8bdb-7d4214af06fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577243} {:answer/id #uuid "646a3baf-7c68-5935-a198-a09a52711555" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577252}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "646a3baf-7c68-5935-a198-a09a52711555" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577252} :answer-field/id #uuid "194c9336-9913-5379-9825-4dba3d9209d2" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577236} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "51c96df9-a022-5711-b0b4-862aa2e02436" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577246} {:answer/id #uuid "57dd76c7-1580-54a7-8702-832f92b56a36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577249}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "57dd76c7-1580-54a7-8702-832f92b56a36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577249} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a0c4a37-dc9b-5b7b-98ce-2b41b1443ec4" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577257} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a1537077-2732-5997-8cda-6940defc768a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577265} {:answer/id #uuid "cdfe72b8-fa2e-56cf-b8f3-590b7c422024" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577273}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a1537077-2732-5997-8cda-6940defc768a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577265} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa93174e-a1e8-55a5-9b08-c1c23b7d6e47" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577268}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "53a41d24-47c9-59a3-bb8f-2ba3ae6870d8" :question/problem "Consider the following differential equation.\n\n$$\ny\\prime=\\frac{3 y}{x},\\qquad x\\ne 0\n$$\n\nLet $f(x)=- 6 x^{2}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $f\\prime(x)=- 24 x.$\n- **II.** Substituting $y=f(x)$ and $y\\prime=f\\prime(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement.\n- **III.** The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation." :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in an interval where the function is defined and the equation is valid.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Differentiating $f(x)=- 6 x^{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f\\prime(x)&=\\left(- 6 x^{2}\\right)\\prime \\\\ &=-6\\cdot 2 x \\\\ &=- 12 x \\\\ &\\not\\equiv - 24 x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Substituting $y=- 6 x^{2}$ and $y\\prime=- 12 x$ into the original equation gives expressions that are not identical:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y\\prime &\\overset{?}{=}\\frac{3 y}{x} \\\\ - 12 x &\\overset{?}{=}\\frac{3\\left(- 6 x^{2}\\right)}{x} \\\\ - 12 x &\\not\\equiv - 18 x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since statement II is false, the function $y=- 6 x^{2}$ is not a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186577251 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100888 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "201edc93-37b4-556a-aaea-4fcf9a01077a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Solution to a First-Order Differential Equation" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049486 :topic/id #uuid "f8bc5d87-e505-5270-9efd-ad77aaf46e52" :topic/math-academy-id 1181 :topic/title "Verifying Solutions of Differential Equations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "012ee319-