df822-8f9a-5e65-ab38-5c493b2f2af9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577258} :answer-field/id #uuid "e98f4f9d-447e-58a2-86b5-8024aca227a8" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577278}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5fd7470a-4c69-539d-97c1-b0bef4d6487e" :question/problem "Consider the following differential equation.\n\n$$\ny\\prime=\\frac{3 y}{x},\\qquad x\\ne 0\n$$\n\nLet $f(x)=- 5 x^{2}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $f\\prime(x)=- 10 x.$\n- **II.** Substituting $y=f(x)$ and $y\\prime=f\\prime(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement.\n- **III.** The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation." :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in an interval where the function is defined and the equation is valid.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Differentiating $f(x)=- 5 x^{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f\\prime(x)&=\\left(- 5 x^{2}\\right)\\prime \\\\ &=-5\\cdot 2 x \\\\ &=- 10 x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Substituting $y=- 5 x^{2}$ and $y\\prime=- 10 x$ into the original equation gives expressions that are not identical:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y\\prime &\\overset{?}{=}\\frac{3 y}{x} \\\\ - 10 x &\\overset{?}{=}\\frac{3\\left(- 5 x^{2}\\right)}{x} \\\\ - 10 x &\\not\\equiv - 15 x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since statement II is false, the function $y=- 5 x^{2}$ is not a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186577256 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/i