gives an identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y\\prime &\\overset{?}{=}\\frac{4 y}{x} \\\\ - 8 x^{3} &\\overset{?}{=}\\frac{4\\left(- 2 x^{4}\\right)}{x} \\\\ - 8 x^{3} &=- 8 x^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statement II is true, the function $y=- 2 x^{4}$ is a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186577294 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100888 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "201edc93-37b4-556a-aaea-4fcf9a01077a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Solution to a First-Order Differential Equation" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049486 :topic/id #uuid "f8bc5d87-e505-5270-9efd-ad77aaf46e52" :topic/math-academy-id 1181 :topic/title "Verifying Solutions of Differential Equations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3fc0976d-8848-5bc7-a8ba-c6fb66573dfe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577288} {:answer/id #uuid "91cca939-abfa-579c-ba0f-76aed088ff08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577306}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "91cca939-abfa-579c-ba0f-76aed088ff08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577306} :answer-field/id #uuid "9baa3746-90cb-500b-8251-3017a1530a1d" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577312} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "acbb8d0f-0fc7-5f97-8c4c-958d8e7cec21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577317} {:answer/id #uuid "ba7030f3-f3be-5e06-ba36-6216c88dadef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/tex