uation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in an interval where the function is defined and the equation is valid.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Differentiating $f(x)=- 2 \\ln{\\left(3 x + 2 \\right)},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f\\prime(x)&=\\left(- 2 \\ln{\\left(3 x + 2 \\right)}\\right)\\prime \\\\ &=-2\\cdot\\frac{3}{3 x + 2} \\\\ &=- \\frac{6}{3 x + 2} \\\\ &\\not\\equiv - \\frac{4}{3 x + 2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Substituting $y=- 2 \\ln{\\left(3 x + 2 \\right)}$ and $y\\prime=- \\frac{6}{3 x + 2}$ into the original equation gives expressions that are not identical:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y\\prime &\\overset{?}{=}- 4 e^{\\frac{y}{2}} \\\\ - \\frac{6}{3 x + 2} &\\overset{?}{=}-4e^{-(- 2 \\ln{\\left(3 x + 2 \\right)})/(-2)} \\\\ - \\frac{6}{3 x + 2} &\\overset{?}{=}-4e^{-\\ln(3 x + 2)} \\\\ - \\frac{6}{3 x + 2} &\\not\\equiv - \\frac{4}{3 x + 2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since statement II is false, the function $y=- 2 \\ln{\\left(3 x + 2 \\right)}$ is not a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186577313 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100888 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "201edc93-37b4-556a-aaea-4fcf9a01077a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Solution to a First-Order Differential Equation" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049486 :topic/id #uuid "f8bc5d87-e505-5270-9efd-ad77aaf46e52" :topic/math-academy-id 1181 :topic/title "Verifying Solutions of Differential Equations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5ac82169-4017-5aee-b8a2-b79e679b0722" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577295} {:answer/id #uuid "ee1fbee2-4889-5e84-9f46-037cf43d3d81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :